## TICKET 1 (P0) — Magnesium Stearate (and any ~24-element page) loses values to JSON truncation

**Confirmed root cause.** The log shows the model's response cut off mid-string:
```
RAW TAIL>>> evel": "~1340",
      ...
      "likely_to_be_present": "Yes", "mrl_value": 98, ...
      "content_measured": "~1340", "report_limit": "98", ...
```
This is the LIGAMED Ni value (`∼1340`, MRL 98) being written correctly, then the JSON stream stopping before it closes — `safe_json_parse` fails, falls back to `{}`, and the entire page contributes zero elements.

**Why now, not before.** `make_ei_prompt`'s per-element schema grew by 5 fields this round to support the regulatory-reference and multi-material fixes: `content_measured`, `report_limit`, `specification_limit`, `regulatory_limit`, `material_name` — on top of the existing ~15 fields. For a ~24-element page, this materially increases output size. But `claude_vision()` in `annexure_converter.py` calls `call_claude()` with no `max_tokens` override, so every per-page EI call is still capped at the old default of 8192 tokens — sized for the smaller pre-expansion schema.

**Fix.**
1. Add a `max_tokens` parameter to `annexure_converter.claude_vision()`, defaulting to the current 8192 so every other call site (metadata, etc.) is unaffected.
2. In `convert_pdf_to_json`, raise `max_tokens` specifically for the per-page `make_ei_prompt` calls (the `run_page_tasks` lambda that calls `claude_vision(_img, make_ei_prompt(...), ...)`) — e.g. 16000 — so a full ~24-element table with the expanded schema always has room to complete.
3. Do NOT shrink the schema back to remove the 5 new fields; they are required for the Option-1/regulatory-reference and multi-material fixes.

**Why this cannot break other documents.** A page with fewer elements or a smaller schema payload simply finishes well under the new ceiling — raising a max is a no-op for any response that was already completing. This only helps a response that was previously running out of room.

**Verify.** Re-run the LIGAMED Magnesium Stearate annexure; confirm no `safe_json_parse failed` warning in the log, and V/Ni/Ba/Cr/Cu/Li reach their correct non-zero values (V≈2.03, Ni≈1.34 µg/g per the source CoA). Spot-check one other multi-element annexure (e.g. IFF, 24+ elements) for the same absence of truncation warnings.

