## TICKET 1 (P0) — USP-classed solvents named with ZERO numeric evidence still form phantom columns

**Confirmed root cause.** Propyl Gallate's declaration (page 8, §7) states: *"does not include the usage of the following ICH Class-1 Solvents in manufacturing: Benzene, Carbon Tetrachloride, 1,2-Dichloroethane 1,1-Dichloroethane, 1,1,1-Trichloroethane."* This is a pure negative-declaration MENTION with no numeric value attached to these four names.

In `process_rs_annexure`, the "exclude if no evidence" gate reads:
```python
is_non_usp = (sinfo is None) or (sinfo.get("class") is None)
if is_non_usp and converted_ppm is None:
    declaration_scopes.append(...); continue
norm_solvents.append(entry)
```
Because Benzene/Carbon tetrachloride/1,2-Dichloroethane/1,1,1-Trichloroethane ARE ICH-classed in `residual_solvent_master.py`, `is_non_usp` is False, so this gate never applies to them — they enter `norm_solvents` with `converted_ppm=None` regardless. Later, `_rs_solvent_disp` creates a column for ANY name that resolves to a canonical master entry, with no check for whether it carries a real value anywhere in the document set. This is why the Sitagliptin run showed these four Class-1 solvents as document-wide assessed columns (all NA except the declaring row) even though not one uploaded annexure states a numeric value for any of them.

**Fix.** Change the exclusion gate to apply regardless of USP/non-USP status when the ONLY evidence is a bare negative-declaration mention with no numeric information:
```python
if converted_ppm is None and etype not in ("negative_declaration", "no_source"):
    declaration_scopes.append(...); continue
norm_solvents.append(entry)
```
A solvent whose evidence IS a proper per-solvent negative-declaration entry (typed `negative_declaration`/`no_source`, which downstream correctly resolves to `converted_ppm=0.0` via the `annexure_limit` negative-declaration branch) is unaffected — this only closes the gap for a USP-classed name mentioned with zero numeric information and no negative-declaration typing.

**Why this cannot break other documents.** A solvent with a real numeric value anywhere (its own annexure or another material's) is untouched — the gate only fires on genuinely empty evidence. A document whose negative declaration IS typed as `negative_declaration`/`no_source` per solvent (the normal path) is unaffected.

**Verify.** Re-run Sitagliptin RS; confirm Benzene/Carbon tetrachloride/1,2-Dichloroethane/1,1,1-Trichloroethane no longer appear as assessed columns (Propyl Gallate's negative statement about them still shows in its declaration_scopes/audit trail, just not as a phantom calculation column). Confirm Ethyl acetate, Ethanol, 1-Propanol (which DO carry real vendor values) are unaffected.

